The issue is that your **`firebaseConfig.ts` file contains placeholder values** (`"YOUR_API_KEY_HERE"`, etc.).

Because the `utils/dataManager.ts` file is trying to connect to a Firebase database using these invalid credentials, the application fails to connect, resulting in "client is offline" or connection errors.

To fix this and make the app work immediately in this preview environment, I will **revert the Data Manager and Auth systems to use Local Storage** (offline database) instead of Firebase.

